      "content": "thanks. it's a bit tricky though because the board is split. some members are saying that keeping things like the Parthenon Marbles or the Benin Bronzes is basically just \"colonialist\" and that it's objectively wrong to hold onto them. then others say that museums are \"universal\" and it's better for science if everything is in one place. \n\ncan you expand on those two points for the draft? like, can you give more detail on the arguments for repatriation and also the arguments for why keeping them in universal museums is important? i want to make sure i'm being thorough.",
